  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The addition polymerisation of acrylonitrile in presence of a peroxide catalyst leads to the formation of polyacrylonitrile. The commercial name of polyacrylonitrile is orlon (acrilan). That is, it is used as a substitute for wool in making commercial fibres as orlon or acrilan.&nbsp;</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0007_c6e3ddbd1d9d.png\" style=\"width: 454px; height: 99px;\" /></p></blockquote>"
